 dialogue:{title:"Correcciones al manuscrito", scene:"Lucía, correctora de estilo, revisa con el novelista Nathan el primer capítulo de su manuscrito.", a:"Lucía", b:"Nathan", lines:[
  ["A","Nathan, before we go any further, I have to flag a dangling participle on page one.","Nathan, antes de seguir, tengo que señalarte un participio colgante en la página uno."],
  ["B","Already? Which sentence?","¿Ya? ¿Qué frase?"],
  ["A","'Driving through the valley, the mountains appeared.' Strictly speaking, the mountains are doing the driving.","'Conduciendo por el valle, aparecieron las montañas'. En sentido estricto, las que conducen son las montañas."],
  ["B","Oh dear. 'Driving through the valley, Elena watched the mountains appear,' then?","Ay, no. ¿Entonces 'Conduciendo por el valle, Elena vio aparecer las montañas'?"],
  ["A","Much better. Now this: 'After the funeral was over and everyone had left, she went upstairs.' It's rather plodding.","Mucho mejor. Ahora esto: 'Después de que terminó el funeral y todos se fueron, subió'. Es bastante pesado."],
  ["B","Could I say 'The funeral over, the mourners gone, she went upstairs'?","¿Podría decir 'Terminado el funeral, idos los dolientes, subió'?"],
  ["A","Exactly. Two absolute clauses, and the rhythm becomes elegiac.","Exacto. Dos construcciones absolutas, y el ritmo se vuelve elegíaco."],
  ["B","I like it. What about the ending of the chapter? I feel it fizzles out.","Me gusta. ¿Y el final del capítulo? Siento que se desinfla."],
  ["A","She opens the drawer and the letter isn't there. Try 'She wrenched open the drawer, only to find it empty.'","Ella abre el cajón y la carta no está. Prueba 'Abrió el cajón de un tirón, solo para encontrarlo vacío'."],
  ["B","'Only to find': yes, that gives it a sting. Anything else?","'Solo para encontrar': sí, eso le da un aguijón. ¿Algo más?"],
  ["A","Here: 'Because she had been warned by her brother, she said nothing.' Why not 'Having been warned by her brother, she said nothing'?","Aquí: 'Como su hermano la había advertido, no dijo nada'. ¿Por qué no 'Advertida por su hermano, no dijo nada'?"],
  ["B","Granted, it's tighter. But won't readers tire of all these participles?","Es cierto que es más compacto. ¿Pero no se cansarán los lectores de tantos participios?"],
  ["A","Fair point. Used sparingly, they quicken the pace; strung together, they choke it.","Buen punto. Usados con moderación, aceleran el ritmo; encadenados, lo asfixian."],
  ["B","So, with the deadline looming, how many pages do we still have to get through tonight?","Entonces, con la fecha límite encima, ¿cuántas páginas nos faltan por revisar esta noche?"],
  ["A","Barring any disasters, about forty. Judging by your face, you'd rather we stopped.","Salvo desastres, unas cuarenta. A juzgar por tu cara, preferirías que paráramos."],
  ["B","That said, I'd rather the book were good. Let's carry on.","Dicho esto, prefiero que el libro sea bueno. Sigamos."]
 ]},
